Check that lld-link behaves like link.exe by default: it does not search for a
Visual Studio install from VCToolsInstallDir or VCINSTALLDIR, and a library
missing from the command line and LIB is not taken from one. /vcautodetect
restores the upstream search. Explicit /winsysroot and LIB keep working.

Limit: the VS setup configuration (COM) and the registry cannot be faked from
lit. The default cases prove those lookups are skipped only on a host with VS,
where they would find one; they sit behind the same guard as the env lookup.

# RUN: rm -rf %t.dir && mkdir -p %t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 %t.dir/oldvc/lib/amd64 %t.dir/empty
# RUN: cp %p/Inputs/std64.lib %t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64
# RUN: cp %p/Inputs/std64.lib %t.dir/oldvc/lib/amd64

Default: VCToolsInstallDir is not consulted, so std64.lib is not found.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   not lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONE --implicit-check-not="VC toolchain:" \
# RUN:     --implicit-check-not="SDK lib path:" \
# RUN:     --implicit-check-not="UCRT lib path:" %s

NONE: LINK : fatal error LNK1181: input file 'std64.lib' was not found

Default: the older-layout VCINSTALLDIR is not consulted either. The lit host may
export VCTOOLSINSTALLDIR (vcvars), which takes precedence, so these cases run
through Inputs/scrub-env.py.
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCINSTALLDIR=%t.dir/oldvc -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONE --implicit-check-not="VC toolchain:" %s

Control: /vcautodetect restores the VCToolsInstallDir search.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /vcautodetect /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND --implicit-check-not="note: lld-link" %s

FOUND: VC toolchain: {{.*}}sysroot{{[/\\]}}VC{{[/\\]}}Tools{{[/\\]}}MSVC{{[/\\]}}1.1.1.1

Control: /vcautodetect restores the VCINSTALLDIR search (older layout).
# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCINSTALLDIR=%t.dir/oldvc -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /vcautodetect /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose > %t.foundold.txt 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUNDOLD %s < %t.foundold.txt

FOUNDOLD: VC toolchain: {{.*}}oldvc

/vcautodetect with LIB set: the environment is consulted and LIB is searched.
# RUN: env LIB=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 \
# RUN:   VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /vcautodetect /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

Explicit /winsysroot works with VS variables set and no /vcautodetect.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/doesnotexist \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsysroot:%t.dir/sysroot \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

LIB is still searched by default.
# RUN: env -u VCTOOLSINSTALLDIR -u VCINSTALLDIR \
# RUN:   LIB=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe

The last of /vcautodetect and /novcautodetect wins, in both orders.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   not lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /vcautodetect /novcautodetect \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONE --implicit-check-not="VC toolchain:" %s
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /novcautodetect /vcautodetect \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

The hint names the cause when a VS variable is set, LIB is not, and the command
line names no library directory. Each of the three VS variables counts.
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=HINT %s
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCINSTALLDIR=%t.dir/oldvc -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=HINT %s
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VSINSTALLDIR=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=HINT %s

HINT: LINK : note: lld-link does not search for Visual Studio by default (like link.exe); set LIB (run vcvars) or pass /vcautodetect
HINT-NEXT: LINK : fatal error LNK1181: input file 'std64.lib' was not found

No hint when LIB is set (the missing library is then a plain LIB problem).
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=NOHINT --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s

No hint when the command line names a library directory: with /libpath the
missing library is a wrong name or a wrong directory.
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /libpath:%t.dir/empty /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NOHINT --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s

No hint with a flag that makes lld-link ignore LIB ("set LIB" cannot help):
/winsdkdir, /vctoolsdir, /winsysroot, /lldignoreenv.
# RUN: mkdir -p %t.dir/sdk/Include/10.0.1.1 %t.dir/sdk/Lib/10.0.1.1/um/x64
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NOHINT --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /vctoolsdir:%t.dir/empty /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NOHINT --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsysroot:%t.dir/empty /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NOHINT --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /lldignoreenv /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NOHINT --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s

NOHINT: LINK : fatal error LNK1181: input file 'std64.lib' was not found

No hint in MinGW mode, which never searched for Visual Studio.
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link -lldmingw %p/Inputs/hello64.obj nosuch.lib /entry:main \
# RUN:   /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=MINGW --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s

MINGW: 'nosuch.lib'
